course: dictionary
lesson: 5005
title: One word, many meanings: infant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary numbers them, but in a real text you need the context, the words around the word, to choose the right one. «At an infant baptism, parents and godparents make promises to bring the child up in the faith.» The words parents, godparents and child show that infant means a baby here. Check by swapping in baby: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The Mole's garden has «plaster statues of Garibaldi, and the infant Samuel, and Queen Victoria, and other heroes of modern Italy». A statue of Samuel as a small child is what the word means here: a very young child. The writer makes a joke, because only Garibaldi was an Italian hero, so read the whole sentence before you decide what a word means.
explain: In UK schools, infant means something different again. The infants are the youngest children in primary school, about ages four to seven, and an infant school is for them. So when someone says «I go to infant school», the context tells you the meaning is about school, not about babies.
fact: Infant means a baby or a very young child, especially one who cannot yet walk or talk well.
fact: In the UK, the infants are the youngest children in primary school, about ages four to seven, and an infant school is for them.
fact: Infant can also describe something new that has just begun, such as an infant company.
fact: Useful phrases: newborn infant, infant formula (special food for babies), infant school.
fact: The stages of life go: infant, child, teenager, adult.
exercise: «At an infant baptism, parents and godparents make promises.» What does infant mean here? | A teenager with a school bag | A school in the north | A grown-up godparent | *A baby
exercise: Ella says, «I go to infant school.» Which ages are the pupils there? | Only babies in prams | *About four to seven | Adults only | About eleven to sixteen
exercise: «The shop is an infant company, only started this year.» What does infant mean in this sentence? | A large, busy factory | A small baby animal | *Something new that has just begun | Very old and famous
test: Which phrase means a baby just born? | *newborn infant | infant company | teenager | infant school
test: The statue shows «the infant Samuel». What kind of person is shown? | A grown man | *A very young child | A sailor | A teenager
exam: Which word comes between infant and teenager in the stages of life? | adult | newborn | *child | school
